# Copilot Agent Plugin — runnable .http examples
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. Control Plane API running locally (default: http://localhost:5149)
#   2. CopilotAgent__Enabled=true set in .env.local
#   3. gh CLI installed with the Copilot extension: gh extension install github/gh-copilot
#   4. gh auth login completed so the extension is authenticated
#
# Secrets: never commit real project IDs or API tokens here.
# Copy this file and override @HOST in your local .env.local or IDE HTTP client settings.

@HOST = http://localhost:5149
@PROJECT_ID = placeholder

###
# Ask Copilot to suggest a shell command for a backend task.
# RequiresConfirmation=true — the UI shows the suggested command for review before commit.
# The returned "suggestedCommand" in the output is for human review only; it is never executed automatically.

POST {{HOST}}/api/operations/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "{{PROJECT_ID}}",
  "operationId": "trigger-copilot-suggest",
  "requestedBy": "engineer@example.com",
  "input": {
    "prompt": "List all running .NET processes on Linux and show their memory usage"
  }
}

###
# Ask Copilot to explain a shell command or error message.
# RequiresConfirmation=false — read-only and non-destructive.

POST {{HOST}}/api/operations/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "{{PROJECT_ID}}",
  "operationId": "trigger-copilot-explain",
  "requestedBy": "engineer@example.com",
  "input": {
    "subject": "dotnet: /usr/share/dotnet/dotnet: cannot execute binary file: Exec format error"
  }
}

###
# Retrieve the last 20 operation executions (includes Copilot Agent history).

GET {{HOST}}/api/operations/history?take=20
Accept: application/json
